**New Evidence**
- EIH launch and mandate as a state wealth-management vehicle.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopian Investment Holding Launch Event","publisher":"Ethiopian Investment Holdings","publication_date":"2022-10-22","url":"https://eih.et/ethiopian-investment-holding-launch-event/","claim":"Ethiopian Investment Holdings held its first conference in Addis Ababa; the finance minister said its mission was to usher in global investment and modern capabilities, and the CEO said it was creating a national team for public wealth management to optimize public assets and deliver critical services.","locator":"lines 52-56","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official launch page with direct statements from senior government officials; strong for formal launch and stated mandate, weaker for actual performance.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022 and describing a June 2022 launch","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy-era executive architecture: the launch and mandate reflect a ruler-backed institutional reform, though not personal operational control over day-to-day SOE management.","contrary_evidence":["Official self-presentation may overstate effectiveness","The page shows intent and setup, not measured results"],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.10"]}

- Abiy-linked economic program was explicit: open telecom, logistics, and finance; manage inflation and private-sector transition.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"With Active Private Participation, Ethiopia's Economy Will Grow More: Senior PM Advisor","publisher":"Ethiopian News Agency","publication_date":"2022-09-07","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_38237","claim":"Mamo Mihretu said the administration was taking progressive reform measures to open the telecom, logistics, and financial sectors, called this the government's declared intention, and said the government was also taking measures on inflation, foreign currency, and essential imports.","locator":"lines 55-70","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official news source quoting the PM adviser and EIH CEO directly; strong for declared policy direction and early implementation claims, weaker for independent verification.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Abiy's administration through his senior policy adviser and EIH chief; this is the clearest revealed program statement for the period.","contrary_evidence":["This is part self-report and part forecast","Inflation and FX stress remained serious, so the claim does not by itself prove success"],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.7","8B.10"]}

- IMF assessed the authorities' 2022 reform agenda as a real policy package under external shocks.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Staff Visit Discusses Reform Plans and Economic Developments in Ethiopia","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-06-21","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/06/21/pr22216-ethiopia-imf-staff-visit-discusses-reform-plans-and-economic-developments-in-ethiopia","claim":"IMF staff said Ethiopia faced multiple shocks, but the authorities aimed to address macroeconomic imbalances, remained committed to structural reforms for a transition to private-sector-led growth, and wanted better public investment efficiency, SOE oversight, debt treatment, FX reform, and monetary modernization.","locator":"press release bullets and quoted statement","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF mission statement with a detailed reform narrative and specific policy pillars.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Ethiopian authorities under Abiy; the package reflects executive ownership, though external shocks and creditor support shape feasibility.","contrary_evidence":["The IMF explicitly noted severe conflict, drought, COVID, Ukraine-war, inflation, and FX constraints","The document is about plans and commitment, not completed reform"],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.3","8B.7","8B.8","8B.10"]}

- Safaricom mobile money licensing shows concrete market-opening implementation.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia grants Safaricom mobile money service licence -finance minister","publisher":"Reuters via MarketScreener","publication_date":"2022-10-06","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/SAFARICOM-PLC-6500172/news/Ethiopia-grants-Safaricom-mobile-money-service-licence-finance-minister-41943756/","claim":"Reuters reported that Ethiopia's finance minister said the government had granted Safaricom a licence to operate a mobile money service, hours after the telecom operator switched on its network in Addis Ababa.","locator":"lines 971-996","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters report with a precise administrative action and named official source.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's government as the licensing authority; this supports execution of the telecom-opening program, though not broader economic success.","contrary_evidence":["A single licence does not prove wider competition or downstream delivery","The article does not show who drove the decision inside government"],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.7"]}

- State-run Ethiopian Airlines posted major FY 2021/22 gains under the EIH umbrella.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopian airlines revenues, profit jump in FY 21/22","publisher":"Reuters via MarketScreener","publication_date":"2022-08-31","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Ethiopian-airlines-revenues-profit-jump-in-FY-21-22-41655941/","claim":"Reuters reported that state-run Ethiopian Airlines posted a 90 percent jump in net profit to 937 million dollars and a 79 percent rise in revenue to 5 billion dollars for FY 2021/22, with lower operating costs and more passengers and cargo.","locator":"lines 819-837","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a major state-owned enterprise with concrete figures and a named holding-company executive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"covers the 2021/22 fiscal year ending in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: the airline sat inside the newly created EIH portfolio, so Abiy's reform architecture gets some credit, but not sole credit for performance.","contrary_evidence":["The airline was already a strong institution and benefited from post-pandemic recovery","EIH leadership, not Abiy personally, is the immediate manager of performance"],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- Abiy and the AU-backed process converted the ceasefire into an implementation roadmap.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia truce implementation to start immediately, mediator says","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","publication_date":"2022-11-12","url":"https://theprint.in/world/ethiopia-truce-implementation-to-start-immediately-mediator-says/1213377/","claim":"Reuters reported that the Ethiopian government and Tigrayan forces signed a roadmap for implementing the peace deal, with implementation to start immediately on humanitarian access, civilian protection, and disarmament.","locator":"Reuters article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on a concrete implementation roadmap with named mediator and specific steps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Shared attribution: the government was a principal signatory and executor, so Abiy's administration clearly owned the government's side of implementation.","contrary_evidence":["The roadmap is not proof of successful follow-through","Implementation remained dependent on both sides and external monitoring"],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- The AU said the parties agreed on humanitarian access and a DDR committee.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Senior Commanders Meeting between the Government of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia and the Tigray Peoples' Liberation Front agree to facilitate unhindered humanitarian access","publisher":"African Union Peace and Security Department","publication_date":"2022-11-12","url":"https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/senior-commanders-meeting-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf-agree-to-facilitate-unhindered-humanitarian-access","claim":"The AU said the parties agreed to facilitate unhindered humanitarian access, security guarantees for aid workers, protection of civilians, and a joint committee for a comprehensive disarmament, demobilization, and reintegration program.","locator":"lines 82-88","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary AU communique with explicit implementation steps and institutional follow-through requirements.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Shared attribution, but it clearly reflects the Ethiopian government's negotiated implementation capacity under Abiy's administration.","contrary_evidence":["Again, this is an agreement, not proof that aid access was fully restored on the ground","The AU language is optimistic and not an audit"],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- Abiy publicly committed to honest implementation of the peace agreement.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia's Abiy says committed to the implementation of agreement","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://theprint.in/world/ethiopias-abiy-says-committed-to-the-implementation-of-agreement/1194158/","claim":"Reuters reported that Abiy told parliament the government was committed to peace and that its commitment to implementing the agreement was strong, saying the next step was to implement honestly what had been promised.","locator":"lines 115-117","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Reuters quote in contemporaneous republishing, good for revealed intent and commitment record.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Abiy; this is a stated commitment rather than a completed outcome, so it mainly establishes the program and willingness to be held to it.","contrary_evidence":["A promise is not performance","Later reports still described implementation gaps and access problems"],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.8","8B.10"]}

- Aid access still lagged after the truce, showing implementation limits.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia says Tigray aid allowed, agencies say still no access","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-11-12","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/12/ethiopia-conflict-aid","claim":"Reuters reported that Ethiopia's government said aid was allowed and ready to move into Tigray, while humanitarian agencies said they were still awaiting access nine days after the truce was declared.","locator":"search result snippet and article summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters report with direct contrast between government claim and agency observation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to the Ethiopian government's implementation performance under Abiy, though some delay also reflected the other side and operational conditions.","contrary_evidence":["The government had formally agreed to aid access and implementation steps","Access delays can reflect battlefield conditions, not just administrative incompetence"],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- Abiy launched a national anti-corruption committee and linked it to new systems and prosecutions.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gov't Establishes National Committee To Coordinate Anti-Corruption Campaign","publisher":"Ethiopian News Agency","publication_date":"2022-11-17","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_40240","claim":"Abiy said the government established a national committee to coordinate the anti-corruption campaign, would bring culprits before court, and was putting in place new systems supported by technologies to prevent corruption.","locator":"lines 55-72","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statement with explicit executive direction and operational framing, though not independent evidence of effectiveness.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Abiy as PM; this is a clear anti-corruption initiative and a concrete administrative response.","contrary_evidence":["Official self-report does not prove even-handed enforcement","No convictions or audit outcomes are shown in the article"],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.5","8B.8"]}

- Abiy appointed Meseret Damtie to head the federal auditor general office.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Executive Is Happy When Taking Budget, But Unhappy When They See Our Auditors","publisher":"The Reporter Ethiopia","publication_date":"2022-12-24","url":"https://www.thereporterethiopia.com/28896/","claim":"The Reporter said Meseret Damtie was chosen by Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed in June 2022 to fill the vacant head of the Office of the Federal Auditor General post and that she brought more than 20 years of public financial administration experience.","locator":"lines 157-160","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Local interview/profile with specific appointment details and professional background, but still secondary reporting rather than a nomination decree.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct appointment by Abiy; this is strong evidence that he empowered a technically experienced oversight head rather than leaving the post vacant.","contrary_evidence":["Appointment quality does not prove independence in practice","The article itself says the executive had a weak response to public financial mismanagement"],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.8"]}

- The same auditor-general interview reported concrete audit follow-through and returned funds.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Executive Is Happy When Taking Budget, But Unhappy When They See Our Auditors","publisher":"The Reporter Ethiopia","publication_date":"2022-12-24","url":"https://www.thereporterethiopia.com/28896/","claim":"The auditor-general said the office returned over 4.1 billion birr that had been unlawfully spent, forwarded multiple mismanagement cases to the Ministry of Justice, and was bringing regional states into a single federal audit system for the first time.","locator":"lines 204-223","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific operational claims in a detailed interview, supported by concrete figures, though still reliant on the auditor-general's account.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful: the result reflects the effect of Abiy's staffing and legal changes on oversight capacity, not personal execution by the PM.","contrary_evidence":["This is a self-described reform success and may overstate independent impact","The article also acknowledges institutional resistance and uneven acceptance"],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.8","8B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I screened roughly 30 documents across Reuters/Euronews syndications, IMF, World Bank/IFC, African Union, Ethiopian News Agency, EIH, The Reporter Ethiopia, WHO, UNICEF, WFP, Le Monde, Xinhua, Addis Standard, and a few 2024 retrospective IMF and World Bank items.
- I kept sources that either stated Abiy's 2022 program directly, showed concrete implementation actions, or gave credible outcome evidence tied to the reform agenda.
- I rejected or downgraded items that were too generic, too far removed from ruler-level execution, or too easy to personalize from country context alone: broad governance indicators, generic conflict/humanitarian descriptions, and documents that showed capacity or need but not ruler-owned action.
- I excluded several 2024 and 2026 retrospective pieces even when useful as background, because the 2022-specific record was already supported by direct 2022 evidence.
- I treated some mirrored Reuters items on syndication pages as one canonical Reuters claim each, rather than padding the dossier with duplicate publishers.
- A few IMF eLibrary pages were blocked at the source level; where relevant I used the accessible IMF press release and search-result summaries instead.

**Remaining Gaps**
- The clearest gap is direct internal evidence of how Abiy himself managed implementation bottlenecks inside ministries, regions, and SOEs beyond public speeches and delegated appointments.
- I still do not have a clean, independent documentary trail for the full Homegrown Economic Reform Agenda by end-2022, especially on what was implemented versus merely announced.
- The SOE and telecom reforms are real and concrete, but attribution is partly indirect: technocrats and state entities did much of the operational work.
- If you want tighter confidence on 8B, the next useful search would be deeper on 2022 budget execution, cabinet reshuffles, and independent assessments of whether the peace implementation roadmap and SOE reforms actually advanced on schedule.

No score produced.
